<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70566" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέω</span></b>  (C), fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Suid.
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνησα</span> (v. infr.):—
				Med.
			, fut. (in pass. sense) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr.): aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνησάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Polyaen.
					8.65
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Pass.
			, aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνήσθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>An.</u>
					7.3.2
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				2.54
			</span></i>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνήθην </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ</span>-) prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				4.2.10
			</span></i>: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νένημαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1522.23
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iv B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i> (v. infr.), perh. also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νένησμαι</span> (v. infr.); 
				Ion.
			
			3pl.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νενέαται </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συν</span>-) <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.135
			</span></i>; 3sg.
			plpf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνένηστο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>VH</u>
					5.6
				</span></i>
			: pres. only in compds. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπι-, περινέω</span> (qq.v.):—<i>heap, pile up,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρὴν νῆσαι</span>
			<i>pile</i> a funeral pyre, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.50
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				269
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
			</span></i> l.c. (
				Pass.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήσαντες ξύλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					243
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφορῆς νενησμένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					1203
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτοι νενημένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					5.4.27
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῶντος,</span> glossed <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σωρεύοντος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be stuffed,</i> c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νενημένην χοῖρον πολλῆς φορίνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.
					4.15
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νησόμεθα: κορεσθησόμεθα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (Contr. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηέω,</span>
		q.v.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
